---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import IntermediateNav from '../../components/IntermediateNav.astro';
import ChapterGoals from '../../components/ChapterGoals.astro';
import TrainingOptions from '../../components/TrainingOptions.astro';
import RouteStep from '../../components/RouteStep.astro';
import ProgressTracker from '../../components/ProgressTracker.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 1.4 · Farming, Desert Treasure & Earth Orbs" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="1-4" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 1.4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Convert the early foundation into a real midgame account.</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">This subsection has four connected payoffs: protection prayers, sustainable Farming Contracts, Ancient Magicks, and a large Earth-orb stock for the Chapter 2 battlestaff cash loop. The quest order below is deliberately linear, with exact future items called out only when they save a meaningful return trip.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="You are finishing the quest/stat web prepared in 1.3 and deliberately preparing the first several Chapter 2 blocks. The major breakpoints are 43 Prayer, 62 Farming, 46 Hunter, Desert Treasure, 108 Paddewwa tablets and 1,590 charged Earth orbs. This subsection also banks the small but easy-to-miss carryovers Chapter 2 expects: mushroom pies, a spare bucket of sap, a harralander, 2,000 stardust and—if birdhouse RNG cooperates—two growing teak trees."
        stats={["70 Woodcutting — 75 only if you still lack 16 magic logs", "43 Prayer · 45 Ranged · 46 Hunter", "40 Herblore · 42 Smithing · 56 Crafting", "62 Farming before boosted medium contracts; about 63 by chapter end", "63 Magic · 77 Thieving", "39 Construction target for the Chapter 2 handoff", "Optional AFK detour: 60 Attack / 60 Strength / 60 Defence"]}
        unlocks={["4 mushroom pies for the Earth-battlestaff bootstrap", "The Grand Tree + Eyes of Glouphrie", "Garden of Tranquillity + Eadgar’s Ruse", "Farming Contracts", "My Arm’s Big Adventure", "Ancient Magicks via Desert Treasure", "108 Paddewwa tablets", "1,590 charged Earth orbs"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Full Chapter 1 finish line:</strong> roughly 46 Attack · 50 Strength · 34 Defence · 39 Hitpoints · 45 Ranged · 43 Prayer · 63 Magic · 24 Runecraft · 39 Construction · 51 Agility · 40 Herblore · 77 Thieving · 56 Crafting · roughly 47–48 Fletching (46 is the deliberate checkpoint) · 16 Slayer · 46 Hunter · 44 Mining · 42 Smithing · 74 Fishing · 60 Cooking · 89 Firemaking · 70 Woodcutting · 63 Farming.</div>

      <TrainingOptions skill="Woodcutting" target="70" why="This is the deliberate skilling break after the dense 1.3 questing. Chapter 1 also needs 16 magic logs; Wintertodt may already have supplied them. At 65 Woodcutting, the route also takes one short Fossil Island detour for a Chapter 2 Crafting boost." recommended="Forestry or normal teak cutting for the bulk of the grind. Once you reach 65 Woodcutting, pause and do Sulliusceps until you have 5 sulliuscep caps, then return to your preferred method to 70." relaxed="AFK the best trees you find comfortable and accept the slower XP rate; the only mandatory detour is obtaining the 5 sulliuscep caps." resource="If you reach 70 and still have fewer than 16 magic logs banked, continue to 75 Woodcutting and cut the missing magic logs yourself." fast="2-tick teaks are faster, but are never required by this guide." />

      <RouteStep id="i14-pies" number="1" title="Turn the Sulliuscep caps into four mushroom pies for Chapter 2">
        <p>Once you have <strong>5 sulliuscep caps</strong>, make <strong>4 mushroom pies</strong> now and leave the fifth cap as a spare. For four pies, bring <strong>4 pie dishes, 4 pots of flour, a jug/bucket of water and 4 sulliuscep caps</strong>.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Use flour with water to make <strong>4 pastry dough</strong>.</li>
          <li>Use each pastry dough on a pie dish to make <strong>4 pie shells</strong>.</li>
          <li>Add <strong>1 sulliuscep cap</strong> to each shell.</li>
          <li>Bake all four on the <strong>Lumbridge Castle range</strong> or another convenient range. Your <strong>60 Cooking</strong> from 1.2 meets the requirement.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Why four?</strong> Earth battlestaves require <strong>58 Crafting</strong>, while this chapter ends around 56. Mushroom pie gives a temporary <strong>+4 Crafting boost</strong>, allowing Chapter 2 to start attaching the first Earth orbs immediately; the Crafting XP from those staves then removes the need to keep boosting.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-gnomes" number="2" title="Complete The Grand Tree, then The Eyes of Glouphrie">
        <p>Complete <strong>The Grand Tree</strong> from start to finish. Then complete <strong>The Eyes of Glouphrie</strong>. These are now one clean Gnome Stronghold quest block rather than quests you started hours ago and periodically revisited.</p>
        <p>After Eyes of Glouphrie, enchant the <strong>crystal saw seed</strong>. Keep the crystal saw; it becomes a useful Construction booster later.</p>
        <p>Before leaving this block, bring a <strong>knife + 1 empty bucket</strong> to an <strong>evergreen tree</strong> (the trees between Barbarian Village and Falador are convenient). Use the knife on the tree with the bucket in your inventory and bank <strong>1 bucket of sap</strong>. Early Chapter 2 needs it for <strong>Icthlarin's Little Helper</strong>; collecting it now prevents an otherwise pointless return trip.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-garden" number="3" title="Complete Garden of Tranquillity and bank the compost with a purpose">
        <p>You already have at least <strong>33 Farming</strong> from the Chapter 1.3 quest rewards and Creature of Fenkenstrain is complete, so do <strong>Garden of Tranquillity</strong> from start to finish now. Bring the <strong>ring of charos</strong> from 1.3.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Farming math:</strong> By this point the route has awarded at least <strong>19,500 Farming XP</strong>: 1,000 from the Goblin generals subquest, 3,500 from Fairytale I, 5,000 from Forgettable Tale, and 10,000 from The Garden of Death. That is at least <strong>level 33</strong>. Garden of Tranquillity adds another <strong>5,000 XP</strong>, so both <strong>Enlightened Journey (30 Farming)</strong> and <strong>My Arm's Big Adventure (29 Farming)</strong> are already covered with no hidden farm run.</div>
        <p>During the Farming work, bank <strong>15 supercompost</strong>. Label the reason mentally:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>7 supercompost are reserved for My Arm’s Big Adventure.</strong></li>
          <li>The remaining <strong>8</strong> are a small Farming/Herblore buffer and can be converted/used normally after My Arm is complete.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you use compost potions for early Herblore, one dose can upgrade a normal compost bin/bucket to supercompost; the volcanic ash from Fossil Island can later turn supercompost into ultracompost.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Start the Chapter 2 teak timer now:</strong> Garden of Tranquillity pushes the guaranteed quest XP past <strong>35 Farming</strong>. If you have the <strong>2 teak seeds</strong> reserved from birdhouses, put each seed in a <strong>filled plant pot</strong> with a gardening trowel, water it, wait for the sapling, then plant the two saplings in the <strong>two western Fossil Island hardwood patches</strong> with a spade. Use <strong>supercompost/ultracompost</strong> on the patches. Teaks take roughly three days to grow, and early Chapter 2 wants two mature player-grown trees for the plank grind. If birdhouse RNG has only given you one or zero seeds, plant what you have and continue birdhouse/Farming Contract runs; Chapter 2 can wait for the remaining tree rather than blocking Chapter 1.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-eadgar" number="4" title="Complete Eadgar’s Ruse and take the two future goutweed now">
        <p>You reached <strong>31 Herblore</strong> in 1.3, so complete <strong>Eadgar’s Ruse</strong> in one pass with no boost required. The quest awards <strong>11,000 Herblore XP</strong>.</p>
        <p>When you reach the goutweed storeroom, collect <strong>3 goutweed total</strong> before leaving. One is used to finish Eadgar’s Ruse; bank the <strong>2 extras</strong> for <strong>Dream Mentor</strong> and <strong>Dragon Slayer II</strong>. This is a worthwhile future pickup because returning to the storeroom is genuinely annoying.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-kourend-easy" number="5" title="Finish Kourend & Kebos Easy and put the 2,500 XP lamp on Herblore">
        <p><strong>Do not grind Herblore to 40.</strong> BruhSailer reaches 40 through guaranteed quest/diary XP plus incidental potion XP. Because this guide only guarantees the exact <strong>31 Herblore</strong> needed for Eadgar’s Ruse, we make the diary lamp explicit so the breakpoint is deterministic.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Guaranteed Herblore math from the minimum route:</strong> level 31 begins at 14,833 XP. <strong>Jungle Potion</strong> in 1.3 adds 775, <strong>Eadgar’s Ruse</strong> adds 11,000, this diary lamp adds 2,500, and <strong>My Arm’s Big Adventure</strong> in the next step adds 10,000. That totals <strong>39,108 Herblore XP</strong>, safely above the <strong>37,224 XP</strong> needed for level 40. Any Wintertodt herbs, lamps or extra potions are simply bonus progress.</div>
        <p>Complete any Easy tasks you have not already done. Bring a <strong>pickaxe, weapon, spade, 8,750 gp, tarromin potion (unf), 1 limpwurt root, fly fishing rod and feathers</strong>. If you do not already have a limpwurt root, kill <strong>Hill Giants</strong> until one drops.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Mine <strong>iron ore at the Mount Karuulm mine</strong>.</li>
          <li>Kill a <strong>Sand Crab</strong>.</li>
          <li>Hand in a <strong>book at the Arceuus Library</strong>.</li>
          <li>Steal from a <strong>Hosidius fruit stall</strong>.</li>
          <li>Browse the <strong>Warrens General Store</strong>.</li>
          <li>Take the boat to <strong>Land’s End</strong>.</li>
          <li>Pray at the altar on the <strong>top floor of Kourend Castle</strong>.</li>
          <li>Dig up <strong>saltpetre</strong> south-west of Hosidius.</li>
          <li>Speak to an <strong>Estate Agent</strong>, move your POH to <strong>Hosidius for 8,750 gp</strong>, then enter it through the Hosidius portal. Leave the house there for now.</li>
          <li>Complete a lap of either <strong>Shayzien Agility Course</strong>.</li>
          <li>In the <strong>Lovakengj pub</strong>, add the limpwurt root to the tarromin potion (unf) to make a <strong>strength potion</strong>.</li>
          <li>Fish a <strong>trout from the River Molch</strong> south-east of the Farming Guild.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Claim <strong>Rada’s blessing 1</strong> and the <strong>2,500 XP antique lamp</strong> from Elise at Kourend Castle. Put the lamp on <strong>Herblore</strong>.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Current-game note:</strong> Kourend Favour was removed in 2024. If an old guide tells you to gain Hosidius/Shayzien favour for these tasks, ignore it; the current Easy diary uses the tasks listed above.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-myarm" number="6" title="Complete My Arm’s Big Adventure and let the quest finish 40 Herblore">
        <p>This is the payoff for the setup already completed: <strong>Eadgar’s Ruse</strong> is done, <strong>The Feud</strong> and <strong>Jungle Potion</strong> are complete, 1.3 banked <strong>100% Tai Bwo Wannai favour</strong>, and the Farming quest rewards already cover the <strong>29 Farming</strong> requirement.</p>
        <p>Bring <strong>3 buckets of Ugthanki dung</strong>, <strong>7 supercompost</strong>, climbing boots or Trollheim teleport access, some coins, and normal combat gear/food. A bucket can be obtained during the quest. The Trollheim tool leprechaun can supply a rake, seed dibber, spade and plant cure when needed.</p>
        <p>Complete <strong>My Arm’s Big Adventure</strong> from start to finish. During the Tai Bwo Wannai section, Murcaily gives you the separate <strong>hardy gout tuber</strong>; this is not the regular gout tuber banked during Cleanup in 1.3.</p>
        <p>The quest awards <strong>10,000 Herblore XP</strong> and <strong>5,000 Farming XP</strong>. Following the minimum XP route above, this is the point where <strong>40 Herblore is guaranteed</strong>. No extra herb-processing grind is required.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Keep the regular gout tuber banked.</strong> My Arm does not consume it. Early Chapter 2 uses it for the <strong>Karamja Medium Diary gem-machete exchange</strong>. Starting My Arm at 100% Tai Bwo Wannai favour leaves you at 40% after the quest spends 60 percentage points.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-smith" number="7" title="Reach 42 Smithing and finish the Chapter 1 jewelry stock">
        <p>Use Blast Furnace or a normal Smithing method to reach <strong>42 Smithing</strong>. Then bring your teleport jewelry up to the full Chapter 1 target:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>40 rings of dueling</strong></li>
          <li><strong>45 digsite pendants</strong></li>
          <li><strong>10 games necklaces</strong></li>
          <li><strong>8 bracelets of clay</strong></li>
          <li><strong>2 sapphire amulets</strong> — turn one into an <strong>amulet of magic</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 ruby amulet</strong> — enchant it into an <strong>amulet of strength</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 binding necklace</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Count what you made in 1.3 and only craft the difference. These quantities are intentionally explicit because the rest of Chapter 1 consumes teleport jewelry heavily.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-family" number="8" title="Complete Family Crest">
        <p>Complete <strong>Family Crest</strong> as a standalone quest. Keep the resulting gauntlet access; the quest is also an important prerequisite for later account progression.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-prayer" number="9" title="Kill 70–80 green dragons, bank every bone, then cash them in for 43 Prayer">
        <p><strong>Yes, the dragon bones are the Prayer method.</strong> This step has two separate halves: first bank the bones and hides from green dragons; then take the bones to the <strong>Wilderness Chaos Altar</strong> in small, disposable inventories until you reach <strong>43 Prayer</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Dragon-killing setup:</strong> take a <strong>games necklace</strong>, <strong>water staff</strong>, <strong>air runes</strong>, <strong>chaos runes</strong>, <strong>mind runes</strong>, <strong>anti-dragon shield</strong>, <strong>amulet of magic</strong>, a <strong>looting bag</strong>, and cheap food such as the banked salmon. Wear only gear you are comfortable losing; do <strong>not</strong> bring your cash stack.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Use the games necklace to teleport to <strong>Corporeal Beast</strong>.</li>
          <li>Leave the cave into the Wilderness and run <strong>west</strong> to the nearby green dragons. The current green dragons have a <strong>50% weakness to Water spells</strong>, which is why this route uses Water Bolt.</li>
          <li>Cast <strong>Water Bolt</strong> while you have a comfortable chaos-rune buffer. <strong>Do not spend your final 100 chaos runes.</strong> When you reach roughly 100 remaining, swap to <strong>Water Strike</strong> and finish the grind with mind runes instead.</li>
          <li>Pick up <strong>every dragon bone and every green dragonhide</strong>. Put the hides into the looting bag first and keep the bones in your inventory; bank before you are carrying a pile you would hate to lose.</li>
          <li>Kill <strong>70 dragons minimum</strong>. The source route recommends continuing to about <strong>80 total</strong> because the Chaos Altar's bone-saving effect is random. This guide uses <strong>80 banked dragon bones</strong> as the clean target unless earlier Prayer XP means you obviously need fewer.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Keep one spare dragon bone banked after reaching 43 Prayer.</strong> Do not blindly empty the bank just because bones remain.</div>
        <p><strong>Turning the bones into Prayer XP:</strong> bank all combat gear. From <strong>Ferox Enclave</strong>, take only <strong>one inventory of dragon bones</strong> at a time and run to the <strong>Chaos Temple in level 38 Wilderness</strong>. Use the bones on the Chaos Altar until the inventory is gone, then return/suicide and repeat. The altar gives the same <strong>350% XP</strong> as a gilded altar with both burners lit and each offered bone has a <strong>50% chance not to be consumed</strong>, so a bone can be offered more than once. Stop immediately when you reach <strong>43 Prayer</strong>; any unused bones stay banked for later.</p>
        <div class="optional-efficiency"><strong>Risk rule:</strong> never carry the whole bone stack into the Wilderness and never bring gear you care about. Losing one disposable inventory is annoying; losing the entire Prayer bank is avoidable.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-imp" number="10" title="Complete Imp Catcher before finishing the Ranged target">
        <p>Check your bank for the four beads: <strong>red, yellow, black and white</strong>. If any are missing, kill imps around the <strong>Tower of Life / Ardougne area</strong> until you have one of each, then complete <strong>Imp Catcher</strong>.</p>
        <p>This is placed here because the Magic XP is still useful and it closes another Chapter 1 quest without creating a special trip later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <TrainingOptions skill="Ranged" target="45" why="Shadow of the Storm already contributed 10,000 Ranged XP in 1.3. Finish the remaining gap here so Temple of Ikov and the remaining quest combat are comfortable." recommended="Gemstone Crab in the Tlati Rainforest. Children of the Sun was completed in 1.2, so Varlamore is already unlocked. Travel to Varlamore, run south into the Tlati Rainforest, and enter any of the three Gemstone Crab mine caves; the caves route you to whichever mine currently has the crab. Bring your best Ranged gear and the knives/darts/arrows you intend to use. The crab effectively has infinite HP and stays in place for about 10 minutes; when it burrows, use the nearby cave to follow it. It gives 12.5% less XP per hit than normal targets, but the long idle windows and lack of overkill downtime make it excellent for this guide's AFK preference." relaxed="Sand Crabs or Ammonite Crabs are still excellent low-attention alternatives if you prefer familiar crab spots. Let quest combat finish the last level or two if you are already close." resource="Loar Shades are valid if you specifically want shade remains, but Chapter 1 does not require them." fast="High-input knife/dart training is optional." />

      <RouteStep id="i14-optional-melee" number="Optional" optional={true} title="Optional AFK break: take melee to 60 Attack / 60 Strength / 60 Defence at Gemstone Crab">
        <p>If you want to front-load combat while doing something almost entirely second-screen, stay at <strong>Gemstone Crab</strong> after 45 Ranged and train melee to <strong>60 Attack, 60 Strength and 60 Defence</strong>.</p>
        <p>Equip the <strong>rune sword</strong> purchased in 1.3, your <strong>amulet of strength</strong>, and the best melee armour already in the bank. Attack the crab, leave auto-retaliate on, and move through the nearby cave when the crab relocates roughly every ten minutes. Train the three melee stats in whatever order you prefer; 60/60/60 is the clean stopping point.</p>
        <div class="optional-efficiency"><strong>This is genuinely optional.</strong> The original Chapter 1 finish line is only about 46 Attack / 50 Strength / 34 Defence. Going to 60/60/60 makes a large amount of Chapter 2 combat more comfortable and is a good use of AFK time, but no following Chapter 1 step assumes you did it.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-journey" number="11" title="Complete Enlightened Journey and A Soul’s Bane">
        <p>Complete <strong>Enlightened Journey</strong> for balloon transport, then complete <strong>A Soul’s Bane</strong>. You are already guaranteed <strong>30 Farming</strong> from the quest XP math in Step 3, so there is no extra Farming grind before Enlightened Journey.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-glass" number="12" title="Final Crafting checkpoint: finish the 1,590 unpowered orbs">
        <p>Part 1.3 already established the full glass plan, and this is the deadline. Your original <strong>1,600 molten glass</strong> should be accounted for as:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1,590 unpowered orbs</strong></li>
          <li><strong>6 molten glass</strong> reserved for <strong>Desert Treasure</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 molten glass</strong> reserved to blow a <strong>lantern lens</strong> for <strong>The Hand in the Sand</strong></li>
          <li><strong>3 spare molten glass</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you chose to split the bankstanding grind across the chapter, <strong>finish every remaining unpowered orb now</strong>. The orb blowing — not merely making the molten glass — is the Crafting XP that brings the route to roughly <strong>56 Crafting</strong>. Do not start the Earth-orb charging block until all <strong>1,590</strong> are ready.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-quests" number="13" title="Complete Biohazard, then Watchtower">
        <p>Complete these as two normal standalone quests, rebanking between them:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Biohazard</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Watchtower</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <p>My Arm’s Big Adventure has deliberately been moved earlier in this page so the <strong>40 Herblore breakpoint is resolved immediately after Eadgar’s Ruse and the Kourend Easy lamp</strong>, rather than being hidden inside an unrelated multi-quest block.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <TrainingOptions skill="Farming" target="62" why="Medium Farming Contracts normally require 65 Farming. At 62 you can use a +3 garden-pie boost to enter the intermediate tier and request medium contracts, giving the account a sustainable long-term seed engine." recommended="Low-attention route: do normal tree, fruit-tree and hardwood runs with the best seeds your account has. It takes more real-world time but very little active play." relaxed="Let Farming happen over several days while you quest, skill and do birdhouses. There is no requirement to sit at Tithe Farm for hours in one session." resource="At 62, make or obtain garden pies and use the +3 boost whenever you need 65 to access/request medium contracts. Plant a whiteberry bush as soon as practical and keep at least 1 white berry for The Hand in the Sand." fast="Tithe Farm is the bounded active option when you want to force the level now. Use any comfortable pattern; optimized tick-perfect Tithe is not assumed." />

      <TrainingOptions skill="Hunter" target="46" why="Birdhouses should already have supplied much of this level. 46 is the Chapter 1 benchmark and leaves the account in a good place for future Hunter content." recommended="Keep doing birdhouse runs until 46 Hunter. If you are only a few levels short, there is no need to force a separate grind." relaxed="Wait for additional birdhouse cycles across normal play sessions." resource="If you want to finish immediately, use a conventional Hunter method appropriate to your level." fast="Kebbit/chinchompa routes are available if you want faster active XP." />

      <RouteStep id="i14-ikov" number="14" title="Complete Temple of Ikov without hunting a yew longbow">
        <p>Bring <strong>20 unnoted limpwurt roots</strong>, a light source, weight-reducing gear, and <strong>darts or throwing knives</strong>. Complete <strong>Temple of Ikov</strong>.</p>
        <p>You do <strong>not</strong> need to grind Puro-Puro for a yew longbow. In the ice chamber, search the chests until you obtain at least <strong>1 ice arrow</strong>. Equip the ice arrow in your ammo slot, then use darts/throwing knives on the Fire Warrior of Lesarkus; the current quest mechanics allow thrown weapons to bypass the normal yew-bow requirement.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-dt" number="15" title="Complete Desert Treasure from start to finish">
        <p>With <strong>The Dig Site, The Tourist Trap, Troll Stronghold, Priest in Peril, Waterfall Quest</strong> and <strong>Temple of Ikov</strong> completed, all quest prerequisites are done. Your Chapter 1 stats also clear the hard gates: <strong>53 Thieving, 50 Magic, 50 Firemaking and 10 Slayer</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Before starting, withdraw or confirm you have:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>12 magic logs</strong>, <strong>6 steel bars</strong> and the <strong>6 molten glass</strong> reserved earlier</li>
          <li><strong>ashes, charcoal, 1 blood rune, bones and 1 silver bar</strong></li>
          <li><strong>garlic + pestle and mortar</strong> for garlic powder, <strong>spice</strong>, and one accepted sweet such as a chocolate bar/cake</li>
          <li><strong>climbing boots + 1 iron bar</strong> so Dunstan can make the spiked boots</li>
          <li>the <strong>gas mask</strong> kept from Plague City, a <strong>tinderbox</strong>, and roughly <strong>30-50 lockpicks</strong></li>
          <li>good food, several prayer/restoration potions, energy potions and antipoison</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Complete <strong>Desert Treasure</strong> from start to finish. The gas mask is the important easy-to-miss item: keep it equipped in the Smoke Dungeon.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>One worthwhile future pickup:</strong> if your Kamil/ice route already gives you easy access to <strong>1 Trollweiss</strong>, bank it for Troll Romance. If getting it would require starting another quest or assembling a separate sled setup, skip it and collect it during Troll Romance later.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-paddewwa" number="16" title="Make all 108 Paddewwa teleport tablets now">
        <p>After Desert Treasure, switch to Ancient Magicks and prepare:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>108 soft clay</strong></li>
          <li><strong>108 air runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>216 law runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Fire staff</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Make <strong>108 Paddewwa teleport tablets</strong>. The Earth-orb grind itself uses only part of this stack, but making the full batch now avoids repeating the spellbook/lectern setup later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <TrainingOptions skill="Construction" target="39" why="Scrambled! has a hard 38 Construction requirement, while the Chapter 1 / early Chapter 2 handoff is cleaner at 39. Getting Ahead and Wintertodt repairs help, but neither guarantees the level, so finish it explicitly here." recommended="Use Mahogany Homes with your banked oak planks until 39. This is the preferred lower-intensity route." relaxed="Break the contracts into short sessions around birdhouse runs or Farming timers." resource="Use existing planks first and buy only what you need to close the gap." fast="Oak larders/furniture in your POH are faster if you want the level immediately." />

      <RouteStep id="i14-varlamore" number="17" title="Finish the Varlamore unlocks and buy the cosmic-rune total">
        <p><strong>Children of the Sun was completed in 1.2</strong>, so the Varlamore chain is ready. Complete <strong>Twilight’s Promise</strong>, then—with <strong>39 Construction</strong> now guaranteed—complete <strong>Scrambled!</strong>. Then use the Tal Teklan rune shop and other existing stock to bring your bank to <strong>4,900 cosmic runes total</strong>.</p>
        <p>The orb batch consumes <strong>4,770 cosmic runes</strong>—three per orb—so 4,900 leaves a small buffer for enchanting and mistakes.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-orbs" number="18" title="Charge all 1,590 Earth orbs with the simple route">
        <p>Use the low-complexity version rather than the gravestone/corpse method:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Equip an <strong>earth staff</strong> and a bank teleport such as a ring of dueling.</li>
          <li>Withdraw <strong>25 unpowered orbs</strong>, <strong>75 cosmic runes</strong> and <strong>1 Paddewwa tablet</strong>.</li>
          <li>Break the Paddewwa tablet and run through Edgeville Dungeon to the <strong>Earth Obelisk</strong>.</li>
          <li>Cast Charge Earth Orb until all 25 are charged.</li>
          <li>Teleport to a bank, deposit the Earth orbs, restock, repeat.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Continue until all <strong>1,590</strong> are charged. This is slower than an optimized death/gravestone storage route, but it is much easier to follow and produces the same Chapter 2 resource.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i14-hand" number="19" title="Complete The Hand in the Sand with the exact inventory">
        <p>Your Farming Contracts should have produced/grown the whiteberry by now. Bring:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>150 coins</strong></li>
          <li><strong>2 empty vials</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Redberries</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 white berry</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 lantern lens</strong> blown from the molten glass reserved earlier in this subsection</li>
          <li><strong>5 earth runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 bucket</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Complete <strong>The Hand in the Sand</strong>. Bert’s daily sand is now unlocked for future glassmaking.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 2 handoff check</div>
        <h3>Do not leave Chapter 1 with an invisible dependency missing.</h3>
        <p>Before moving into the Intermediate Chapter 2 route, confirm the following bank/state. These are the Chapter 1 resources that become relevant early enough in Chapter 2 that collecting them here is worthwhile:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1,590 charged Earth orbs</strong></li>
          <li><strong>4 mushroom pies</strong> (plus the spare fifth sulliuscep cap if you still have it)</li>
          <li><strong>2,000 stardust</strong>, unspent, for the Celestial ring</li>
          <li><strong>At least 100 chaos runes</strong> still banked; the green-dragon step deliberately swaps to Water Strike instead of consuming this reserve</li>
          <li><strong>At least 1 spare molten glass</strong>; the 1,600-glass batch leaves three spare after 1,590 orbs + 7 reserved quest glass, and early Chapter 2 calls for one</li>
          <li><strong>1 regular gout tuber</strong> from Tai Bwo Wannai Cleanup; this is a required Chapter 2 carryover for the Karamja Medium machete exchange</li>
          <li><strong>1 harralander</strong> reserved for Heroes' Quest</li>
          <li><strong>1 bucket of sap</strong> reserved for Icthlarin's Little Helper</li>
          <li><strong>10 buckets of slime</strong> from 1.2; early Chapter 2 uses most of them around the Ectofuntus/Ghosts Ahoy sequence</li>
          <li><strong>15 salmon</strong> reserved from the Fishing section for the later Myreque quest chain</li>
          <li><strong>Heavy fishing rod</strong> kept from Barbarian Training; Chapter 2 returns to Barbarian Fishing</li>
          <li><strong>2 teak trees planted/growing</strong> in the western Fossil Island hardwood patches if seed RNG allowed it</li>
          <li><strong>Kharedst's memoirs</strong>, <strong>crystal saw</strong>, <strong>gas mask</strong>, <strong>rune sword</strong>, green d'hide chaps/vambraces and your teleport jewelry</li>
          <li><strong>2 spare goutweed</strong> banked for much later quest use</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The Intermediate route does <strong>not</strong> require Dragon Slayer I, Monkey Madness I, Black Knights' Fortress, Death to the Dorgeshuun, Underground Pass or Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl to be partially started. Chapter 2 will start and finish those in coherent blocks instead of assuming partial quest state.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 1 complete</div>
        <h3>The account now has a midgame backbone.</h3>
        <p>You now have passive Hunter, fairy rings, Farming Contracts, protection prayers, Ancient Magicks, a practical teleport network, the exact early-Chapter-2 carryovers above, and <strong>1,590 Earth orbs</strong> ready for the battlestaff/alchemy money loop.</p>
      </section>

